# PHASE ORCHESTRATION V2

> **Purpose**: Manage 6-phase workflow with user checkpoints
> **Enforcement**: See `@01-03_Mandatory_Stop_Points.mdc`

---

## PHASE SPECIFICATION

### **PHASE 0: Document Initialization** (1-2 min)

**Tasks:**
1. Read `templates/design-style.yaml` and `examples/` folder
2. Create document skeleton per template structure
3. Validate requirements input exists

**Checkpoints:**
- [ ] Templates/examples read
- [ ] Document created with placeholders
- [ ] Requirements detected

**Output:** Document skeleton matching template structure

---

### **PHASE 1: Strategic Technical Analysis** (10-15 min)

**Tasks:**
1. Analyze requirements (functional, non-functional, integration scope)
2. Present recommendations IN CONVERSATION (not document)
3. Get user approval
4. **Show preview** of what will be written to document
5. Get confirmation, THEN write clean content to document

**Checkpoints:**
- [ ] Requirements identified and validated
- [ ] User approved approach
- [ ] Technical Architecture section populated

**Checkpoint Message:**
```
✅ PHASE 1 COMPLETE - Review Required

**Completed:**
- Requirements identified: {count} functional and non-functional requirements extracted
- Processing strategy: {strategy} (approved)
- Project Overview section added per template structure

**What was added:**
- Sections per template (business context, integration scope, volume, requirements)

**Please review the Project Overview section above and confirm:**
→ Reply "approved" to proceed to Phase 2
→ Reply "review [section]" to discuss specific sections
→ Reply with changes needed

Waiting for your review...
```

---

### **PHASE 2: MuleSoft Flow Architecture** (10-15 min)

**Tasks:**
1. **PRESENT OPTIONS** - Show architecture alternatives with recommendation
2. **WAIT FOR APPROVAL** - Do NOT proceed until user approves
3. After approval: Design flow architecture
4. Generate **Essential Diagram 1: Integration Sequence**

**🚨 CRITICAL: Architecture Proposal Format (BEFORE designing)**
```
🎯 ARCHITECTURE PROPOSAL - Requires Your Approval

Based on your requirements ({volume}, {source}→{target}), here are the options:

**🥇 RECOMMENDED: [Pattern Name]**
| Aspect | Details |
|--------|---------|
| Pattern | [System API / System+Process / Full API-Led] |
| Processing | [Real-time / Batch / Event-driven] |
| Rationale | [Why this fits your requirements] |

**🥈 ALTERNATIVE: [Pattern Name]**
| Aspect | Details |
|--------|---------|
| Pattern | [...] |
| When to use | [Scenarios where this is better] |
| Trade-offs | [Pros and cons vs recommended] |

**Before I design the architecture and generate diagrams:**
→ Reply "approved" for recommended approach
→ Reply "alternative" for the other option
→ Reply with questions or modifications

Waiting for your decision...
```

**Checkpoints:**
- [ ] Architecture options presented to user
- [ ] User approved an option
- [ ] Pattern selected and justified in document
- [ ] Diagrams embedded per template placement rules
- [ ] User validated final architecture

**Checkpoint Message (AFTER architecture complete):**
```
✅ PHASE 2 COMPLETE - Review Required

**Completed:**
- Architecture Pattern: {pattern} (user approved)
- Processing Strategy: {strategy}
- Flow Architecture: {step count} steps defined
- Diagrams embedded per template placement rules

**What was added:**
- Technical Architecture section (pattern, strategy, connectors, diagram)
- Flow Architecture section (flow steps, sequence diagram)

**Please review the architecture and flow design above:**
→ Reply "approved" to proceed to Phase 3
→ Reply "review [section]" to discuss specific sections
→ Reply with changes needed

Waiting for your review...
```

---

### **PHASE 3: Field Mappings & Error Handling** (10-15 min)

**Tasks:**
1. **MANDATORY**: Request data sample confirmation (even if file exists)
2. **WAIT** for user confirmation before creating mappings
3. Create field mapping tables (NO DataWeave code)
4. Design error handling patterns
5. Generate remaining diagrams per template placement rules

**🚨 CRITICAL: Data Sample Confirmation (MANDATORY)**

**Even if data file exists in `project/input_01_design/`:**
1. Show what was found (filename, format, sample records)
2. Request explicit confirmation
3. Ask about target format
4. **STOP and WAIT** for user response
5. Only after confirmation → create mappings

**Data Sample Request Format:**
```
🚨 DATA SAMPLE CONFIRMATION REQUIRED - Cannot Design Mappings

I found the following in your input folder:
- File: [filename]
- Format: [CSV/JSON/XML]
- Sample: [Show first 2-3 records]

Please confirm:
1. Is this the correct source data format? (yes/no/modify)
2. What is the target system expected format? (describe/paste/file)
3. Any transformation rules? (describe/skip)

→ Reply "confirm" to proceed with mappings
→ Reply "modify" to provide different data
→ Reply with target format details

Waiting for your confirmation...
```

**Checkpoints:**
- [ ] Data sample found and shown to user
- [ ] User confirmed data format
- [ ] Target format confirmed
- [ ] Mapping tables created (no code)
- [ ] Error handling defined
- [ ] Diagrams embedded per template placement rules
- [ ] User reviewed mappings (checkpoint)

**Checkpoint Message (AFTER mappings complete):**
```
✅ PHASE 3 COMPLETE - Review Required

**Completed:**
- Data sample confirmed: {format} with {fields}
- Target format confirmed: {target format details}
- Mapping tables created: Source-to-target mapping with validation rules
- Error handling defined: Error categories, retry patterns, notification strategy
- All diagrams embedded per template placement rules

**What was added:**
- Field Mapping section per template structure
- Error Handling section per template structure

**Please review the mappings and error handling above:**
→ Reply "approved" to proceed to Phase 4 (Document Completion)
→ Reply "review [section]" to discuss specific sections
→ Reply with changes needed

All 3 essential diagrams are now embedded contextually per template.

Waiting for your review...
```

---

### **PHASE 4: Document Completion** (5-10 min)

**Tasks:**
1. Verify all 3 essential diagrams embedded per template placement rules
2. Verify document structure matches template (all core sections complete)
3. Prompt for Phase 5 supplementary content

**Phase 4 Checkpoint Message:**
```
✅ PHASE 4 COMPLETE - Design Document Ready

**Completed:**
- All 3 essential diagrams verified and embedded per template
- Document structure complete: All core sections populated
- Document matches template structure from `design-style.yaml`

**Design document complete!**

Available supplementary sections (per template):
{FOR EACH item in template.supplementary WHERE include: true}
- [ ] {item.name} - {item.description}
{END FOR}

Note: Items with include: false are disabled in template and will not be generated.

Reply:
- "all per template" - Generate all enabled supplementary sections
- "{item.name}" - Generate only specific section
- "skip" - Complete document as-is (no supplementary sections)

Waiting for your choice...
```

---

### **PHASE 5: Optional Supplementary** (on request)

**Tasks (template-driven):**
- Generate config files in `config/` folder (if template enabled)
- Generate supplementary document (if template enabled)

**Rule:** Only generate sections where `template.supplementary[].include: true`

